WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
A large language model, or LLM, edited just 0.016% of a small model's weights. The edit raised a math benchmark from 7.9% to 48.1%. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 223. Zyphra's Sparse Attention Retrofit, Deep Principles, Open Scientific Model, and Linear B's Studio for Coding Agents Follow. Then Things to Try. Researchers at MIT's Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence Lab

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:35.680
laboratory, or CSAILE, showed a general-purpose LLM can read a smaller network's weights

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.820
as text, identify what it was trained to do, and rewrite those weights from natural

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:44.980
language instructions, with no gradient descent and no retraining.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:53.720
GPT-6 ASTRA, Analytics India Magazine Reports, received only the 17,253 raw weights of each

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:57.900
of four identical architecture networks, and correctly named every game.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:03.600
Those networks had been trained on breakout, pong, Pac-Man, and Freeway, and the same

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:12.980
model also wrote new networks from scratch. On QN 3.50.8B, it lifted GSM 8K from 13.8%

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:22.720
to 67.1%, and IFA Val, an instruction following benchmark, from 21% to 62.3%. The weight changes

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:27.640
is mainly shut down repetitive reasoning loops. They did not add new mathematical ability.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:35.200
Rikia Takehi, Jaden Teo, Alex Zhang, and Omar Qatab published the work November 2nd, and

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:40.749
it is still preliminary and has not been peer-reviewed. Zyfra Hierarchical Attention, or

00:01:40.749 --> 00:01:47.789
ZHA, is a sparse attention method from Zyfra AI that retrofits frozen LLMs with a hierarchical

00:01:47.789 --> 00:01:53.529
tree index. Mark TechPost says the design reaches subquadratic scaling, so cost grows

00:01:53.529 --> 00:01:59.049
slower than the square of sequence length. After 4 billion tokens of distillation, the

00:01:59.049 --> 00:02:05.129
approach matches dense attention on reasoning and 256,000 retrieval benchmarks. It remains

00:02:05.129 --> 00:02:12.844
compatible with existing model weights. Hydrogen 1.0 arrived from deep principle as a 753 billion

00:02:12.844 --> 00:02:19.364
open-weight scientific model. It was post-trained from Z.AI's GLM 5.3 on chemistry,

00:02:19.984 --> 00:02:25.164
material science, and life sciences data, plus laboratory records and agent trajectories.

00:02:25.664 --> 00:02:32.144
The model reports a frontier science research win over GPT-6 astra and ships under the MIT license.

00:02:33.297 --> 00:02:38.377
Linear B launched a Genetic Studio to feed context to engineering leaders and coding agents.

00:02:38.377 --> 00:02:44.037
The platform turns software delivery telemetry into a knowledge graph that both humans and agents

00:02:44.037 --> 00:02:45.617
can query in plain language.

00:02:46.317 --> 00:02:47.077
CityBiz reports.

00:02:47.937 --> 00:02:53.597
Early users report that AI-assisted pull requests are now 2.6 times larger at the 75th

00:02:53.597 --> 00:02:54.197
percentile.

00:02:54.677 --> 00:02:57.277
Yet review wait times have grown more than fivefold.

00:02:57.837 --> 00:03:02.357
A new effort skill layer matches agent compute to change risk and business impact.

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:07.850
Regulated industries that need governed, observable agent deployments are the audience

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:14.470
for Krabo's AI's public beta of its enterprise-grade agent infrastructure platform. Voice of ASEAN

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:21.165
says that is the scale the offering is aimed at. Smare from EBIX and Intentix discovers agents inside

00:03:21.165 --> 00:03:27.465
enterprise systems and establishes accountability baselines. Unite AI says it flags when observed

00:03:27.465 --> 00:03:33.445
behavior deviates from approved business purpose, even when credentials remain valid. EBIX will

00:03:33.445 --> 00:03:39.099
integrate the engine for insurance, financial services, and health care clients. Celestia

00:03:39.099 --> 00:03:44.379
launched Voyager, a payment chain claiming 21 million transactions per second, or TPS,

00:03:44.959 --> 00:03:50.259
for AI agent micropayments. TechFlow says the architecture decouples payment execution

00:03:50.259 --> 00:03:56.179
from consensus and uses a paralyzed lightweight state machine for the high-frequency low-value

00:03:56.179 --> 00:04:02.336
transactions expected from autonomous agents. Hugging face proposed model integration contracts

00:04:02.336 --> 00:04:05.276
or MIC for fast regression testing.

00:04:05.676 --> 00:04:09.716
The standard package is a tiny fixture model, a runnable usage example,

00:04:10.256 --> 00:04:14.736
and human-reviewed baseline outputs so runners on CPU can catch integration bugs

00:04:14.736 --> 00:04:19.656
on every pull request without full graphics processing unit, or GPU suites.

00:04:20.196 --> 00:04:24.396
The UMT-5 bug that allowed decoder look-ahead was caught by such a fixture

00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:26.316
after it had lived in Maine for weeks.

00:04:26.316 --> 00:04:35.633
Simon Willison shipped LLM 0.37 with new open AI compatible endpoint support and GPT 6.1 models.

00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:40.573
The release adds GPT 6.1 sole and GPT 6.1 Terra,

00:04:41.073 --> 00:04:43.893
switches the default to the cheaper GPT 6 Luna,

00:04:44.313 --> 00:04:49.393
and improves embedding handling for mixed content types such as Gemini embedding 2.12.

00:04:49.973 --> 00:04:54.133
Contributors almost all using AI assistance landed fixes in the update.

00:04:54.133 --> 00:05:01.919
A searchable map of 10 years of machine learning papers is live as atlas.skim.ai from reddits

00:05:01.919 --> 00:05:03.219
machine learning community.

00:05:03.609 --> 00:05:11.919
Every accepted paper from ICML, NURRIPS, ICLR, CVPR and AI since 2016 was grouped into

00:05:11.919 --> 00:05:19.199
1,260 topics and results tables and ablations were extracted from 79,000 full texts.

00:05:19.199 --> 00:05:25.219
posts. Each topic page shows benchmark records over time, which baselines recent papers actually

00:05:25.219 --> 00:05:30.979
compare against and direct links to the source papers. CarPathy demonstrated one-promp browser

00:05:30.979 --> 00:05:36.199
extension creation with Claude code, a single instruction to create and deploy an extension

00:05:36.199 --> 00:05:41.139
that shows YouTube thumbnails from halfway through the video, with a toggle produced a working

00:05:41.139 --> 00:05:49.063
extension. Elsewhere, OpenAI raised its bug bounty maximum to $172,000, and partnered with

00:05:49.063 --> 00:05:54.843
cathedral systems on AI-assisted security research, with the new ranges applying retroactively

00:05:54.843 --> 00:05:59.303
to the past 30 days, and more than quadrupling rewards for critical findings.

00:06:00.063 --> 00:06:05.543
Heimstadt and deployed chat GPT Enterprise and Codex across European residential property

00:06:05.543 --> 00:06:10.143
management, and reports cost reductions and employee empowerment from the rollout.

00:06:10.783 --> 00:06:14.583
Andthropic opened applications for its paid research residency program.

00:06:14.583 --> 00:06:21.303
In academics, technical founders and staff-level engineers can apply by November 22nd, with no

00:06:21.303 --> 00:06:26.903
machine learning background required. OpenAI introduced LifeVal, a benchmark for everyday

00:06:26.903 --> 00:06:32.743
personal assistant tasks derived from chat GPT user feedback, covering child care, government

00:06:32.743 --> 00:06:40.857
services, and personal finance scenarios. Point LLM 0.37 at GPT-6 Luna on an embedding job

00:06:40.857 --> 00:06:46.197
that mixes text with audio or images, and check the updated mix content type handling.

00:06:46.677 --> 00:06:52.657
On atlas.skim.ai, pull the topic page for a domain you work in, and note the baselines

00:06:52.657 --> 00:06:56.777
recent papers actually compare against before you choose a reference implementation.

00:06:57.477 --> 00:07:02.977
Put linear B's early access effort skill on a live pull request queue, and watch how it

00:07:02.977 --> 00:07:05.097
sizes agent compute to change risk.

00:07:05.097 --> 00:07:10.617
Run hugging faces model integration contract fixture recipe against a model you maintain

00:07:10.617 --> 00:07:15.357
on CPU so integration regressions get caught before they reach main.

00:07:16.243 --> 00:07:21.983
OpenAI is expected to widen lifevowl and publish detailed task level breakdowns in the coming weeks.

00:07:22.483 --> 00:07:26.223
Andthropic will announce residency decisions after applications close.

00:07:26.903 --> 00:07:31.603
Hugging faces gathering community feedback on the model integration contract specification

00:07:31.603 --> 00:07:34.523
before it names the format a recommended standard.

00:07:34.523 --> 00:07:41.395
Static batches stall a GPU until the slowest sequence finishes, so pop the hood on continuous

00:07:41.395 --> 00:07:42.035
batching.

00:07:42.475 --> 00:07:46.195
New requests join an in-flight batch as soon as earlier sequences finish.

00:07:46.855 --> 00:07:51.775
The key engineering move is dynamic key value cache management, where each request keeps

00:07:51.775 --> 00:07:56.755
its own key value cache slice that can be appended to on the fly, while the attention mask

00:07:56.755 --> 00:07:58.955
is recomputed for the current active set.

00:07:59.475 --> 00:08:03.775
That removes the classic constraint that all requests must finish together and replaces

00:08:03.775 --> 00:08:08.615
This is it with a scheduler that decides at every step which sequences to run and which

00:08:08.615 --> 00:08:09.055
to pause.

00:08:09.635 --> 00:08:13.055
The throughput gain is largest when request lengths vary widely.

00:08:13.615 --> 00:08:18.175
A fleet seeing a mix of short chat turns and long document summaries can reach two to

00:08:18.175 --> 00:08:22.755
four times higher tokens per second than static batching at the same model size.

00:08:23.375 --> 00:08:28.495
The tradeoff is added scheduling overhead and more complex memory fragmentation because

00:08:28.495 --> 00:08:31.695
the key value cache is no longer a single contiguous block.

00:08:31.695 --> 00:08:40.735
Most production servers therefore combine continuous batching with page detention or blockwise cache allocation to keep fragmentation under control.

00:08:41.355 --> 00:08:56.195
Use continuous batching when average request length is short relative to the model context and arrival rate is high and fall back to static or semi-static batching when requests are uniformly long or when strict per request latency service level agreements dominate.

00:08:56.195 --> 00:09:05.315
Cache eviction policies must be tuned per workload, an aggressive eviction rule that works for chat can silently drop long context retrieval sessions.

